## Findings Scorecard

### ✅ F1 — Binary `isConstrained` Conflates Device and Network — **DONE**

**Before:** Single `isConstrained` boolean merged network + device into one flag.
**After:** [perfHints.ts L166-171](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#L166-L171) — Independent [classifyNetworkTier()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#104-126) and [classifyDeviceTier()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#127-142) functions produce separate `networkTier` and `deviceTier` values. `isNetworkConstrained` and `isDeviceConstrained` are derived from tier rank ≥ CONSTRAINED. `isConstrained` kept as backward compat (`isNetworkConstrained || isDeviceConstrained`).

```typescript
const isNetworkConstrained = TIER_RANK[networkTier] >= TIER_RANK.CONSTRAINED;
const isDeviceConstrained = TIER_RANK[deviceTier] >= TIER_RANK.CONSTRAINED;
```

---

### ✅ F2 — No Continuous Scaling — Only 2 Tiers — **DONE**

**Before:** `!hints.isConstrained ? base : base * multiplier` — 2 tiers.
**After:** Full 5-tier system with `INSTANT | FAST | MODERATE | CONSTRAINED | MINIMAL`. Each tier has distinct behavior profiles across polling, flushing, prefetch, retry, hydration, and reconnect.

[perfHints.ts L322-336](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#L322-L336) — [pollIntervalForTier()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#322-337):
| Tier | Effective Poll |
|------|---------------|
| INSTANT | ≤200ms |
| FAST | ≤500ms |
| MODERATE | ≥1,500ms |
| CONSTRAINED | 2× base, min 4,000ms |
| MINIMAL | 3× base, min 6,000ms |

---

### ✅ F3 — WebSocket Reconnect Ignores Own Library — **DONE**

**Before:** Hardcoded `reconnectInterval: 1500`, `reconnectAttempts: 50`.
**After:** [LiveUpdatesProvider.tsx L28-29](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/live/LiveUpdatesProvider.tsx#L28-L29):
```typescript
const reconnectInterval = wsReconnectBaseDelayMs(hints, performanceSettings);
const reconnectAttempts = wsReconnectAttempts(performanceSettings);
```
- Uses [usePerfHints()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#263-266) for reactive tier detection
- [wsReconnectBaseDelayMs()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#433-450) scales by network tier: INSTANT 0.34×, FAST 0.67×, MODERATE 1×, CONSTRAINED/MINIMAL 2×
- [wsReconnectAttempts()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#429-432) capped at 30 via [resolvePerformanceSettings()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#275-321) (clamp 1-30)

