### ✅ F5 — Quote Flush Throttled Incorrectly — **DONE**

**Before:** `hints.isConstrained ? 500 : 250` — network and device conflated.
**After:** [perfHints.ts L338-351](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#L338-L351) — [flushIntervalForTier()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#338-353) uses **`deviceTier`** (not `networkTier`):
```typescript
export function tierFlushIntervalMs(hints, settingsInput) {
  const settings = resolvePerformanceSettings(settingsInput);
  return flushIntervalForTier(hints.deviceTier, settings.quoteFlushIntervalMs);
}
```
Fast device + slow network → 50ms flush (device can render quickly).
Slow device + fast network → 400-1000ms flush (device needs breathing room).

---

### ✅ F6 — One-Shot Prefetch, Not Capability-Aware — **DONE**

**Before:** All 9 or 3 chunks, always sequential, no defer.
**After:** [routePrefetch.ts L90-109](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/routePrefetch.ts#L90-L109) — [tierPrefetchPlan()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#372-399) drives scheduling:
| Tier | Chunks | Mode | Delay |
|------|--------|------|-------|
| INSTANT | 9 | parallel (if device also INSTANT) | 0ms |
| FAST | 9 | sequential | 0ms |
| MODERATE | 6 | sequential | 3,000ms |
| CONSTRAINED | 3 | sequential | 5,000ms |
| MINIMAL | 0 | none | — |

Also supports admin `prefetchStrategy: "all" | "critical" | "none"`.

---

