## Architecture Quality Notes

### Strengths

- **Clean separation of concerns:** Network tier and device tier classified independently, combined only at the final step
- **Typed throughout:** [PerformanceTier](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#4-5), [PerfHints](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#16-30), [PerformanceSettings](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#7-15), [PrefetchPlan](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#31-36) — no `any` types in the public API
- **Reactive by default:** [usePerfHints()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#263-266) + `useSyncExternalStore` means tier changes propagate automatically
- **Graceful degradation:** [resolvePerformanceSettings()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#275-321) clamps all inputs, falls back to safe defaults on parse errors
- **Admin-ready:** Every tier function accepts optional `settingsInput` parameter — the admin config slot is pre-wired
- **SW manifest-driven:** Pre-caching uses the Vite build manifest, not hardcoded chunk names — survives chunk name changes across builds
- **Cache versioning:** `CACHE_NAME` includes `BUILD_HASH` — stale caches purged on deploy via [activate](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/server/routes/admin.ts#1617-1661) handler

### Minor Observations

1. **[ConfigSync.tsx](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/live/ConfigSync.tsx) unchanged** — It correctly invalidates `/api/global-settings` on WS event, which triggers [usePerformanceSettings()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/hooks/use-performance-settings.ts#9-21) refetch. No explicit `updateAdminPerfConfig()` call needed since consumers use hooks that re-read settings on invalidation. This is cleaner than the earlier approach.

2. **[recommendedPollIntervalMs()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#469-475) retained as alias** — [perfHints.ts L469-474](file:///wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#L469-L474) aliases [tierPollIntervalMs()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#354-363). Same for [recommendedQuoteFlushIntervalMs()](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/lib/perfHints.ts#476-479). Forward-compatible — old callers still work.

3. **`build: { manifest: true }`** in vite.config.ts — This generates the `.vite/manifest.json` that [sw.ts](file://wsl.localhost/Ubuntu/home/bcodex/TD.2.ANTIGRAVITY/client/src/sw.ts) reads during install. The two features (manualChunks + manifest) work in concert.

